ALVA — MASH COMBO UPDATE

New Universal Combat Mechanic, Strict Fighter Requirements, CPU Integration, and Animation System Fixes

PRIMARY OBJECTIVE

Implement a completely new universal combat feature called Mash Combo in ALVA.

A Mash Combo activates when a fighter rapidly presses the same eligible grounded close-range melee attack button five times.

Upon successful activation, the fighter automatically performs an extremely fast, visually enhanced, 12-turn attack sequence consisting of exactly two designated grounded close-range melee attacks alternating with one another.

Each attack must be performed six times, producing 12 total attack activations.

During this sequence, all attacks except the final one must have an effective Base Launch of 0. The 12th and final attack must restore its original Base Launch to deliver its proper finishing launch.

Mash Combos must be non-cancellable through ordinary player inputs but interruptible by legitimate enemy attacks and forced combat states.

This mechanic must work for every playable fighter, every supported input device, and CPU-controlled fighters.

Also investigate and permanently fix the existing issue where character animations occasionally become stuck on a single frame.

EVERY RULE INTRODUCED HERE IS A NEW STRICT RULE.

This update is additive. It must not replace, remove, or fundamentally rewrite Alva’s established combat mechanics.

