PART 10 — FIX ANIMATIONS GETTING STUCK ON ONE FRAME

There is an existing problem where certain character animations occasionally get stuck on a single frame.

Investigate this independently of Mash Combo and implement a proper engine-level fix.

Do not cover up the bug by continuously resetting every animation.

Critical investigation area

Inspect:

js/game/rendering/sprite-animator.js

In particular, inspect the logic in SpriteAnimator.play() that skips playback changes when stateKey has not changed.

Also inspect:

* Fighter.updateState()
* Fighter.startAttack()
* Fighter.animationFor()
* CombatState.endAttack()
* CombatState.interruptAttack()
* EnsembleAnimator.play()
* Sprite fallback and frame-hold behavior.
* Animation startup and recovery timing.
* Impact-freeze handling.

Likely failure mechanism

When an attack starts again using the same animation key, the renderer may treat it as the same animation session and refuse to restart at frame zero.

This can leave the sprite displaying the last frame of the previous activation.

The problem may also appear when a new attack replaces another activation without the logical attack state changing.

Verify this failure mode through tests or reproduction before treating it as the only cause.

Required fix

Introduce reliable animation-activation identity or an equivalent restart mechanism.

A new attack activation must restart its corresponding animation correctly, even if:

* The fighter remains in the logical attack state.
* The new move has the same animation key.
* The same button is pressed again after an attack finishes.
* A legitimate hit-cancel begins another attack.
* A Mash Combo advances to another turn.
* A Mash Combo alternates rapidly between two animations.
* A CPU initiates the attack.
* The fighter is an ensemble.

Each new attack should restart once when its activation begins, not once every update frame.

Do not introduce flickering by resetting an animation continuously.

Preserve legitimate animation holds

Differentiate between a genuine stuck animation and an intentional held frame.

The following must continue behaving correctly:

* Single-frame idle or falling poses.
* Shield hold animations.
* Authored static frames.
* Legitimate recovery-frame holds.
* Hitstop or impact freeze.
* Non-looping clips that intentionally hold their final frame until the current move ends.

Fix unintended permanent or incorrect frame holds without breaking these expected behaviors.

Additional validation

Investigate whether any animation becomes stuck because of:

* Missing or invalid frame data.
* Invalid animation FPS.
* Mismatched animation duration and combat duration.
* Incorrect animation state priority.
* A stale animation key after interruption.
* Incorrect pause/resume behavior.
* A stuck attack record.
* Missing animation restart when a new activation starts.
* Broken ensemble member synchronization.

After any interruption, the character must transition into the proper hurt, launch, falling, or idle animation.

After Mash Combo, it must return to normal playback.

The animation bug fix must improve the entire game, not just the new Mash Combo.

